<!-- ================= PHILOSOPHY ================= -->
<section class="sec" id="why">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="sec-head rv">
      <div class="sh-top"><span class="sec-no">(03)</span><span>THE POINT</span><span class="sh-rule"></span></div>
      <h2>Less digging. <em class="grad">More remembering.</em></h2>
      <p class="sec-sub">Same folders. Same photos. A completely different way to stumble upon your favorite moments.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="terms">
      <div class="term bad rv">
        <div class="t-bar"><span class="dot"></span>your photos, as folders</div>
        <div class="t-body">
<span class="tline" style="--d:.05s">~/photos/</span>
<span class="tline" style="--d:.5s">├── summer-road-trip/</span>
<span class="tline" style="--d:.95s">├── old-phone-backup/</span>
<span class="tline" style="--d:1.4s">└── random-memories/</span>
<span class="tline t-dim" style="--d:1.85s">open a folder → open a photo → go back</span>
<span class="tline t-dim" style="--d:2.3s">everything organized, some moments forgotten</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="term good rv" style="--d:.1s">
        <div class="t-bar"><span class="dot"></span>your photos, in Foldergram</div>
        <div class="t-body">
<span class="tline">your library → <span class="t-pr">a personal feed</span></span>
<span class="tline" style="--d:.5s">Recent · Rediscover · Random</span>
<span class="tline" style="--d:.95s">scroll the moments you forgot you saved</span>
<span class="tline" style="--d:1.4s">Reels · Stories · Explore · Collections</span>
<span class="tline" style="--d:1.8s">same photos, same folders, <span class="t-pr">more joy</span> ▮</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <blockquote class="pull rv"><span class="pull-line">“You didn't save those memories to forget them.</span><span class="pull-line grad">Give your memories a way back into your day.”</span></blockquote>
    <p class="after rv">Foldergram doesn't replace your file manager. It gives the photos and videos you already own a familiar place to browse: folders become profiles, photos become posts, and old favorites resurface in the feed. Behind the scenes it uses a local SQLite index and separate previews while keeping local originals in place. You can even include additional drives or an optional read-only Immich source. <strong>Your collection was already yours. Now it feels alive.</strong></p>
  </div>
</section>
